apps/desktop/README.md:23:The host keeps its selected port across restarts. This preserves the renderer origin and its local drafts. A port conflict fails with a link to the host log.
apps/desktop/README.md:25:Close a window to detach its view. Quit Trellis to close the desktop process. Both actions keep the host and agents active. Use the Help menu to reconnect to the host or open its logs.
apps/desktop/README.md:27:The Desktop section of the Settings page holds the data directory and Open Trellis at login. **Trellis > Settings…** (Command-comma) opens that section. The menus keep Open Trellis, Quit Trellis, Quit Trellis Completely, and the Help items. Quit Trellis Completely and the Help items work when the Settings page cannot load.
apps/desktop/README.md:33:The packaged app enables its background service at startup. `SMAppService` registers the bundled LaunchAgent. macOS starts it at login and restarts it after a crash. System Settings controls its permission to run at login. The separate Open Trellis at login switch controls the desktop window.
apps/desktop/README.md:39:The host starts HTTP before it resolves the user login environment. External tools await the cached environment in their server thread. The shell has a ten-second limit. The bundled executable directory comes first in PATH. Shell errors omit captured output because startup scripts can expose secrets.
apps/desktop/README.md:45:Use **Trellis > Restart** to load the installed package. A changed package restarts the host. It keeps a runtime that uses the same protocol. A protocol change stops the runtime before the new host starts.
apps/desktop/README.md:76:The command signs native host binaries and the app with the "Trellis Local Signing" certificate from the login keychain. It recalculates the host release hash before it seals the outer app. It then verifies the nested signatures and the complete app.
apps/desktop/README.md:78:The first run on a machine creates the certificate: a self-signed code signing certificate with a 100-year validity. The import gives `/usr/bin/codesign` access to the private key, so the keychain shows no prompt. The certificate has no trust setting, and codesign signs with it by its SHA-1 hash. Keep the certificate in the login keychain. A new certificate changes the signature of every later build.
apps/desktop/README.md:86:When the packaged app opens its window, it checks for Full Disk Access. It reads `~/Library/Application Support/com.apple.TCC/TCC.db`, which macOS protects without a prompt. Without the grant, Trellis shows one dialog that lists the protected folders that agents read and opens the Full Disk Access pane of System Settings. A granted app never shows the dialog. "Do not ask again" writes `full-disk-access-declined` in the Trellis application data directory; delete the file to see the dialog again.
apps/desktop/README.md:93:The SRE handles all eligible Deploy Queue tickets with one build, install, and restart for the batch.
apps/desktop/README.md:94:The SRE saves a release checkpoint before restart and verifies restored sessions afterward.
apps/desktop/README.md:108:The command signs the local package. It copies the app with `ditto` into a temporary directory beside `~/Applications/Trellis.app` and verifies its signature. It publishes the copy through an atomic directory exchange when an installed app exists. It verifies and stages the host release before a restart. Deleted source files cannot remain in the installed bundle. The running app and its services stay open during the copy.
apps/desktop/README.md:112:Restart Trellis to activate the installed build. A changed package restarts the host and keeps a compatible runtime active. A runtime protocol change stops the runtime. Trellis preserves ticket assignments.
apps/desktop/README.md:122:The app retains earlier releases. The release identity includes the desktop launcher, preload bridge, service launcher, native helper, and LaunchAgent configuration. An unknown service state blocks activation.
apps/desktop/README.md:124:Runtime files stay outside the host database directory, so a database export does not include application binaries. A package replacement does not remove the files of an active runtime. The integration test removes the source app, retains a live PTY, starts another child with the pinned native modules, and restarts the host.
